The canon is CC0 because it was first published that way: every canon/
document was released under this repository's CC0 root license in April 2026,
before the reserved regime was introduced, and a CC0 grant cannot be revoked.
ADR-036 (2026-09-01) corrected the annotation to say what was actually
granted. The reserved lore lives in the numinia-lore repository.

Where REUSE.toml declares no license for a path, no rights are granted:
all rights reserved.

Grandfather clause. Until 2026-08-16 (through commit 0157be9) this
repository was published with a root CC0-1.0 license. That waiver is
irrevocable for the versions published under it and is not revoked or
narrowed by this notice; it does not extend to versions published after
that commit. See LEGAL_DEBT.md for the record.

